msgid "**Chair.** The IAM line (`feature/iam-profile-rbac`) chairs the ERPNext structure. GUI, Security and store-i18n announce every change to the ERPNext structure to the chair before it lands, and a conflict in `roles/web-app-erpnext` resolves by this document."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Changed**"
msgstr "**Spremenjeno**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Changed:** Default distribution switched to *Debian* and CI image handling aligned. Python baseline raised: *dev-python* installs Python 3.11+ by default; *requires-python* raised to *>=3.11*. Cross distro Python interpreter and pip handling unified via *sys-pip-install*. Dashboard deployment uses fixed image *ghcr.io/kevinveenbirkenbach/port-ui:1.0.0* and mounts generated *config.yaml* read only. Alerting hardened with explicit timeouts for compose and email, plus portable mailer and systemd instance fallbacks."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Changing a password changes it everywhere.** A user declares how its password must be generated, the inventory pins one for every declared user, a new generator produces API-key shapes, the deploy rotates credentials between its two passes, and a reset command exists. Applications that persist an administrator password at install now realign it when the declared one changes: Nextcloud, Moodle, EspoCRM, Jellyfin, Listmonk, Discourse, Checkmk, xWiki, n8n, Matrix and the dedicated MariaDB and Postgres engines. Checkmk keeps a 401 fatal so a wrong password cannot lock the account out."
msgstr "**Sprememba gesla ga spremeni povsod.** Uporabnik izjavlja, kako je treba ustvariti geslo, inventar zaponke eno za vsakega prijavljenega uporabnika, nov generator proizvaja API-Key oblike, razporeditev vrti poverilnice med njegovimi dvema prehodoma, in reset ukaz obstaja. Aplikacije, ki vztrajajo geslo skrbnika pri namestitvi ga zdaj prerazporedite, ko se prijavljena spremeni: Nextcloud, Moodle, EspoCRM, Jellyfin, Listmonk, Discourse, Checkmk, xWiki, n8n, Matrix in posvečene MariaDB in motorje Postgres. Checkmk ohranja 401 Usodno, zato napačno geslo ne more zakleniti računa."

msgid "**Channel contract:** Messages are addressed to agent accounts or human usernames, never to session names (``utils.orchestrator.channels``). Matrix is the first channel, email through ``sys-svc-mail`` the second, Zammad the third, in the priority the deployment enables."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Channel contract:** Messages are addressed to agent accounts or human usernames, never to session names (`utils.orchestrator.channels`). Matrix is the first channel, email through `sys-svc-mail` the second, Zammad the third, in the priority the deployment enables."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Checks precede the grant:** The admission checks run inside the agent role before it deploys, so a refusal prevents the embodied container rather than following it."
msgstr "**Pregledi pred donacijo:** Preverjanje sprejema poteka v vlogi zastopnika, preden se uporabi, zato zavrnitev prepreči vsebovano posodo in ne sledi njej."

msgid "**Chips are set by core (screenshot round 1).** port-ui offers only a generic chip API that renders small badges on a tile; the lock and the health badge are Infinito.Nexus logic in core JavaScript that sets those chips at runtime. Whether the locks and the health badges show is an inventory switch each."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Chips**: ``templates/javascript/chips.js.j2`` sets the locks and badges through port-ui’s chip API (``window.portui.chips``); port-ui only renders them."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Chips**: `templates/javascript/chips.js.j2` sets the locks and badges through port-ui's chip API (`window.portui.chips`); port-ui only renders them."
msgstr ""

msgid "**ClamAV runs fail-open with short milter timeouts** so mail keeps flowing while clamd warms its signature database instead of blocking the DATA stage."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Clarifying questions only at the start.** Any open question, ambiguity, or missing decision (e.g. how the worker join tokens are persisted, exact NFS export options per distro, how the per-role `DEPLOYMENT_MODE: compose` opt-out is plumbed, exact placement-constraint shape for the swarm-without-nfs warning path, exact openresty `upstream` resolution syntax for swarm-internal DNS) MUST be raised once at the very beginning of the run, in a single batched question round, BEFORE any file is changed. Once those questions are answered, the agent MUST NOT pause for further clarification. Additional ambiguities discovered mid-run MUST be resolved by the agent using its best judgement, recorded in the affected role's `README.md` or a code comment, and revisited only at PR review."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Claude Code extension:** The image install step pulls the Claude Code extension from Open VSX at build time, so every workspace ships with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Claude profiles:** ``addons.claude-code.config.profiles`` creates named native editor profiles and installs Claude into each. Each entry specifies ``name``, ``mode`` (``gateway`` or ``subscription``), ``model``, and ``context_tokens`` (an integer or ``null``). Gateway profiles require a model; subscription profiles use the saved Claude login. Set ``config.user_data_dir`` to the editor’s absolute data directory and ``config.gateway_url`` to the gateway root URL. The key comes from the Claude role’s existing credentials."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Claude profiles:** `addons.claude-code.config.profiles` creates named native editor profiles and installs Claude into each. Each entry specifies `name`, `mode` (`gateway` or `subscription`), `model`, and `context_tokens` (an integer or `null`). Gateway profiles require a model; subscription profiles use the saved Claude login. Set `config.user_data_dir` to the editor's absolute data directory and `config.gateway_url` to the gateway root URL. The key comes from the Claude role's existing credentials."
msgstr ""

