# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**LDAP federation:** When ``svc-db-openldap`` is present, Zammad authenticates and provisions accounts against the central LDAP."
msgstr "**Zveza LDAP:** Kdaj ``svc-db-openldap`` je prisoten, Zammad Overovitve in obračuni rezervacij proti centralni LDAP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**LDAP federation:** When `svc-db-openldap` is present, Zammad authenticates and provisions accounts against the central LDAP."
msgstr "**Zveza LDAP:** Kdaj `svc-db-openldap` je prisoten, Zammad Overovitve in obračuni rezervacij proti centralni LDAP."

msgid "**LDAP federation:** when ``svc-db-openldap`` is present, Frappe’s LDAP Settings doctype is auto-configured. Its search string admits only members of the three role groups; every LDAP sign-in syncs the roles from the group entries under ``LDAP.DN.OU.ROLES`` (``groupOfNames``, ``member``) and writes first name, last name, phone and mobile from the directory (``LDAP.USER.ATTRIBUTES``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP federation:** when `svc-db-openldap` is present, Frappe's LDAP Settings doctype is auto-configured. Its search string admits only members of the three role groups; every LDAP sign-in syncs the roles from the group entries under `LDAP.DN.OU.ROLES` (`groupOfNames`, `member`) and writes first name, last name, phone and mobile from the directory (`LDAP.USER.ATTRIBUTES`)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**LDAP import, export and Multi edit finish again in LAM.** The Content Security Policy blocked the inline script that checks on LAM's background jobs, so these tools stayed \"in progress\" forever. That script is allowed again."
msgstr "**LDAP uvoz, izvoz in Multi urejanje znova konča v LAM.** Varnostna politika vsebine je blokirala interno skripto, ki preverja LAMTa orodja so ostala. \"v teku\" Za vedno. Scenarij je spet dovoljen."

msgid "**LDAP login:** With the ``ldap`` method on (SSO off and ``svc-db-openldap`` present), Semaphore’s login form binds against the central OpenLDAP directory (``SEMAPHORE_LDAP_*``). The form is then LDAP-only: Semaphore cannot tell local from LDAP accounts at the form, so no local account signs in, the break-glass account included."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP login:** With the `ldap` method on (SSO off and `svc-db-openldap` present), Semaphore's login form binds against the central OpenLDAP directory (`SEMAPHORE_LDAP_*`). The form is then LDAP-only: Semaphore cannot tell local from LDAP accounts at the form, so no local account signs in, the break-glass account included."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**LDAP native** (the user record + roles/contact groups), gated on `svc-db-openldap`, so the `X-Remote-User` (Keycloak `preferred_username`) resolves to a real Checkmk user."
msgstr "**Domorodni LDAP** (zapis uporabnikov + vloge/kontaktne skupine), zaklenjeno `svc-db-openldap`, torej `X-Remote-User` (Keycloak `preferred_username`) se odloči za resnično Checkmk uporabnik."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**LDAP plugin** works on **every client** (web + native Android/iOS/TV/desktop apps)."
msgstr "**Vstavek LDAP** deluje na **vse stranke** (spletna + domača Android/iOS/TV/desktop aplikacije)."

msgid "**LDAP profile fields:** the import copies the login, first name, last name, email, phone, mobile, department, street, postal code, city, country and description (into ``note``) from the ``LDAP.USER.ATTRIBUTES`` keys (``ZAMMAD_LDAP_USER_ATTRIBUTES``). Zammad keeps street, zip, city and country as inactive user attributes, so the API returns them but the user form does not show them."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP profile fields:** the import copies the login, first name, last name, email, phone, mobile, department, street, postal code, city, country and description (into `note`) from the `LDAP.USER.ATTRIBUTES` keys (`ZAMMAD_LDAP_USER_ATTRIBUTES`). Zammad keeps street, zip, city and country as inactive user attributes, so the API returns them but the user form does not show them."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP profile image:** an account the LDAP plugin creates takes the directory photo (``jpegPhoto``) as its avatar, and `files/python/photo_sync.py <./files/python/photo_sync.py>`__ pushes a changed photo to the existing account as a host hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP profile image:** an account the LDAP plugin creates takes the directory photo (`jpegPhoto`) as its avatar, and [files/python/photo_sync.py](./files/python/photo_sync.py) pushes a changed photo to the existing account as a host hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP role gate:** The LDAP search filter only finds members of the ``administrator``, ``operator`` and ``user`` role groups (``memberOf`` under the roles OU), so a directory account without one of them cannot sign in through the form."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP role gate:** The LDAP search filter only finds members of the `administrator`, `operator` and `user` role groups (`memberOf` under the roles OU), so a directory account without one of them cannot sign in through the form."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP role groups:** the LDAP import maps the RBAC role groups ``cn=web-app-zammad-<role>`` under the roles OU onto the same Zammad roles as ``ZAMMAD_RBAC_ROLE_GRANTS`` (``ZAMMAD_LDAP_GROUP_ROLE_MAP``). A directory user in none of them gets Zammad’s signup role (``Customer``), so any directory user can open tickets. The import is the leading source for the roles of every directory user: it runs at deploy, on Zammad’s own LDAP schedule and from the admin panel’s LDAP integration."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP role groups:** the LDAP import maps the RBAC role groups `cn=web-app-zammad-<role>` under the roles OU onto the same Zammad roles as `ZAMMAD_RBAC_ROLE_GRANTS` (`ZAMMAD_LDAP_GROUP_ROLE_MAP`). A directory user in none of them gets Zammad's signup role (`Customer`), so any directory user can open tickets. The import is the leading source for the roles of every directory user: it runs at deploy, on Zammad's own LDAP schedule and from the admin panel's LDAP integration."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP user directory:** KIX' `Auth::LDAP` and `Auth::Sync::LDAP` modules are wired against `svc-db-openldap`, with one backend per role group and one shared sync (`KIX_LDAP_SYNC` in `vars/main.yml`). On every sign-in KIX creates or updates the contact from LDAP: first name, last name, email, login, title, phone, mobile, street, postal code, city, country and the description as comment, all read from the `LDAP.USER.ATTRIBUTES` keys."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP user directory:** KIX’ ``Auth::LDAP`` and ``Auth::Sync::LDAP`` modules are wired against ``svc-db-openldap``, with one backend per role group and one shared sync (``KIX_LDAP_SYNC`` in ``vars/main.yml``). On every sign-in KIX creates or updates the contact from LDAP: first name, last name, email, login, title, phone, mobile, street, postal code, city, country and the description as comment, all read from the ``LDAP.USER.ATTRIBUTES`` keys."
msgstr ""

msgid "**LDAP vCards:** With LDAP enabled, ``mod_vcard`` reads every vCard from the directory: ``FN``, ``GIVEN``, ``FAMILY``, ``EMAIL``, ``NICKNAME``, ``TEL`` and ``PHOTO`` come from the matching ``LDAP.USER.ATTRIBUTES``. Users cannot edit them in their client."
