msgid "**Variants:** [meta/variants.yml](./meta/variants.yml) defines three variants, each with `tor` on. Variant 0 enables every service but `docs` and adds `web-app-gitea` and the `deploy` block of the foreign-server deploy (see **Test variant**). Variant 1 disables every service but `docs`, whose round replays the instructions of this README. Variant 2 enables `ldap` only, so the login form binds against the directory. Variants 0 and 2 also deploy `web-app-lam`, the application the app-control specs pause and resume."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Variants:** `meta/variants.yml <./meta/variants.yml>`__ defines three variants, each with ``tor`` on. Variant 0 enables every service but ``docs`` and adds ``web-app-gitea`` and the ``deploy`` block of the foreign-server deploy (see **Test variant**). Variant 1 disables every service but ``docs``, whose round replays the instructions of this README. Variant 2 enables ``ldap`` only, so the login form binds against the directory. Variants 0 and 2 also deploy ``web-app-lam``, the application the app-control specs pause and resume."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Verbose Debug Logging (stderr-only)**"
msgstr "**Besedno razhroščevanje (samo stderr)**"

msgid "**Verification.** Every change passes `make quality-high` and a minimal compose deploy against the running stack: `make compose-deploy apps=<role> variant=0 disable=<every disableable service except design>` (default `initialize` mode, no teardown, single pass, no `full_cycle`). CSS and branding iterations run without a redeploy through `make design-sync app=<role> variant=0` (re-renders shared CSS, role `style.css` and the generated logo assets). A changed `design.js`, task, template or `meta/` file runs through `make compose-role-sync role=<role> variant=0`, which re-runs only the app role against the running stack and renders the CSP hash in the vhost with it. A role pass runs `make test` and the lint targets of the file types it touched after its last edit, and closes with a role sync and the complete role spec; a pass that changed provisioning runs that role sync twice, and the second run reports no change for the tasks it added. `make quality-high` runs once per two or three role passes, at every merge of the main branch and before a role is committed. Each role is also asserted with one further base color, blue `#001f3f`, through `base=` on the sync targets. Swarm verification is out of scope."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Verified:** ``nft -c`` rejects a fragment before it is written, and the loaded table is read back and refused when it carries no chain. A table that exists is not a rule that runs, so the policy itself is proven by the role that owns it."
msgstr "**Preverjeno:** ``nft -c`` zavrne fragment, preden je zapisan, naloženo mizo pa se prebere nazaj in zavrne, ko ne nosi verige. Razpredelnica, ki obstaja, ni pravilo, ki deluje, zato je sama politika dokazana z vlogo, ki jo ima."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Verified:** `nft -c` rejects a fragment before it is written, and the loaded table is read back and refused when it carries no chain. A table that exists is not a rule that runs, so the policy itself is proven by the role that owns it."
msgstr "**Preverjeno:** `nft -c` zavrne fragment, preden je zapisan, naloženo mizo pa se prebere nazaj in zavrne, ko ne nosi verige. Razpredelnica, ki obstaja, ni pravilo, ki deluje, zato je sama politika dokazana z vlogo, ki jo ima."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Verify and Validate:** Depending on your Pixelfed's configuration, especially if email verification is required, you might need to perform additional steps to verify new accounts or modify user details."
