msgid "A link to the dashboard with the ``#logout-everywhere`` fragment. The dashboard uses only the user’s own access token: it lists the user’s applications through the Keycloak Account REST API, revokes the offline token of every application with offline access, ends every other session of the user, and then runs “Log out on this device”."
msgstr ""

msgid "A link whose label is its own target's filename is a path, not prose: ``[11_oidc.yml](../../group_vars/all/11_oidc.yml)`` would come back with a translated filename. A label that says something about the target keeps its translation, so ``[the OIDC defaults](../../group_vars/all/11_oidc.yml)`` is still sent."
msgstr ""

msgid "A lint keeps `meta/forms.yml` and the role's convergence in step: every field the role converges is declared, and every declared field is converged."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A list of external links relevant to the software or the deployment. Link text MUST be a descriptive label or the domain name. Never use the full URL."
msgstr "Seznam zunanjih povezav, pomembnih za programsko opremo ali uporabo. Besedilo povezave MORA biti opisna oznaka ali ime domene. Nikoli ne uporabite celotnega URL- ja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A literal ``shared: false`` (not a Jinja expression) is the role author pinning an engine the central provider cannot serve. Honouring it is only safe on a manager-pinned role, where the volume stays node-local and the sidecar carries the matching placement constraint."
msgstr "Dobesedno ``shared: false`` (ni Jinja izraz) je vloga avtorja, ki pripenja motor, ki ga osrednji ponudnik ne more opravljati. Spoštovanje je varno le pri vlogi, ki jo vodi vodja, kjer količina ostane v bližini vozlišča in priključek nosi ustrezno omejitev umeščanja."

#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "A literal, optionally piped through ``labelled``, is itself; ``entity_name`` is the role's entity; a name resolves through the template's last ``{% set %}`` before *pos*, the role's variables, or every literal the template passes to it as a macro keyword. Anything else stays the expression, which no reach contains."
