msgid "Leases: the instance renews one lease by heartbeat. When it expires (crash, lost machine, teardown), a live-side reaper revokes the instance's tokens, app passwords and Matrix devices and returns its claimed work packages to `Approved`. `make agents-stop` only suspends; a teardown revokes. Every write re-checks the instance's lease and claim first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Leave `KEEP_NEWEST_PER` and `INCLUDE_PATHS` unset to cancel every matching run, as the lifecycle events do — a closed PR and a deleted branch have no run left that deserves to survive. A fallback also mirrors whatever gates its group: `global-ci-*` cancels on every ref except `main` (where only a `Release version ` head commit cancels), so the push job carries the same predicate and does not listen on `main`, leaving the release case to the group, while `pr-ci-*` is declared `cancel-in-progress: true` unconditionally, so the pull request job is ungated too."
msgstr ""

