msgid "The site name has no setting of its own upstream: `server.js` sets `site_name` once at start from `actorInfo.displayName || 'Postmarks'`, and `actorInfo` comes only from `/app/account.json`, whose presence switches Postmarks into fediverse mode (`src/util.js`). The image build therefore patches that line through `files/javascript/patch_site_name.js` to read `SITE_NAME` instead, rendered from the design label (the role name while `design` is off), so the page title, the header and both Atom feed titles carry it; the role ships no `account.json`, so the display name the patch drops was never set. The OpenSearch description keeps `Postmarks` (`ShortName` in `src/routes/opensearch.js`, the `title` of the search link in `src/pages/layouts/main.hbs`). Option: propose an upstream `SITE_NAME` setting that works without `account.json`, e.g. `process.env.SITE_NAME || actorInfo.displayName || 'Postmarks'` in `server.js`, and drop the patch once the built ref carries it."
