msgid "Today most role specs gate their authenticated scenarios on `sso` (the unified service that replaced `oidc`, see archived requirement 021 in the [README](README.md#archive)) only, even when the role's `meta/services.yml` also declares `ldap.enabled` and a dedicated LDAP auth plugin / driver is wired in. Consequence: a deploy with `disable=sso` (LDAP-only mode) makes every authenticated scenario `skip`, leaving the LDAP path untested. The matrix-deploy variant lists in `meta/variants.yml` typically include an LDAP-only variant exactly to exercise that branch (see e.g. [web-app-opencloud/meta/variants.yml](../../roles/web-app-opencloud/meta/variants.yml), whose variant 2 sets `ldap.enabled: true` with `sso.enabled: false`), but the corresponding spec scenario does not exist yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Today the runner image of `web-app-semaphore` is built from `SOFTWARE_IMAGE:SOFTWARE_IMAGE_TAG` plus the `semaphore` binary of the server image ([files/runner/Dockerfile](../../roles/web-app-semaphore/files/runner/Dockerfile)), and on a development stack that base image is the checkout built as `dev-<git-sha>`. Every deploy that pulls Semaphore in as a provider rebuilds both for each new commit, measured at about 375 s and 7 GB per application deploy."
